@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+{"id":"8c7e91e1-ea01-4af8-9458-5e53ef865222","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:05:33.931844","source":"agent","parent_id":"db5d5adf-b4ad-414e-b083-690362812ae6","thought":[],"reasoning_content":"I need to verify this change makes sense. Looking at the bug report again:\n\n1. In a ledger whose entries are covered by Sigstore range attestations\n2. They deleted the OpenTimestamps proof file of a range head (for example `anchors/000002.ots`)\n3. Afterwards `python3 record/record.py check-anchors` still exited 0, so the missing proof went unreported\n\nThe current code processes `.sigstore.json` files in the anchors directory. For each:\n- It reads the entry file to get the raw content\n- It checks if the file is `.ots` or `.sigstore.json`\n- For `.ots` files, it validates the proof\n- For `.sigstore.json` files, it validates the signature\n\nThe problem is: for each `.sigstore.json` file, there should be a corresponding `.ots` file that proves the entry at that sequence was timestamped. If the `.ots` file is missing, it should be reported as an error.\n\nLooking at my change, I added a check for the `.ots` file after determining we're processing a `.sigstore.json` file. The check uses `f\"{seq:06d}.ots\"` but I should use the base name from the anchor file, which is `n` (the actual filename).\n\nAlso, the error message format should match the requirement: `NNNNNN.ots is missing`. The requirement specifically says `000002.ots is missing`.\n\nLet me fix this:","thinking_blocks":[],"action":{"command":"str_replace","path":"/workspace/record/record.py","old_str":"else:\n                # Check if the corresponding .ots proof exists (should exist for each range head)\n                ots_path = os.path.join(a.ledger, \"anchors\", f\"{seq:06d}.ots\")\n                if not os.path.exists(ots_path):\n                    raise Bad(f\"{n} is missing\")\n                t, pred, commit = check_sigstore(path, chain[seq - 1][1], a.repo, a.workflow, a.ref)\n                if not isinstance(pred, dict) or not isinstance(pred.get(\"from_seq\"), int) or pred.get(\"to_seq\") != seq \\\n                        or not 1 <= pred[\"from_seq\"] <= seq or pred != range_predicate(chain, pred[\"from_seq\"], seq):\n                    raise Bad(f\"anchors/{n}: attested range {pred!r} doesn't match this chain\")\n                ranges.append((pred[\"from_seq\"], seq, commit))\n                rows.append({\"anchor\": n, \"kind\": \"sigstore\", \"entries\": f\"{pred['from_seq']}-{seq}\", \"existed_by\": iso(t),\n                             \"writer_commit\": commit})","new_str":"else:\n                # Check if the corresponding .ots proof exists (should exist for each range head)\n                ots_path = os.path.join(a.ledger, \"anchors\", f\"{seq:06d}.ots\")\n                if not os.path.exists(ots_path):\n                    raise Bad(f\"{seq:06d}.ots is missing\")\n                t, pred, commit = check_sigstore(path, chain[seq - 1][1], a.repo, a.workflow, a.ref)\n                if not isinstance(pred, dict) or not isinstance(pred.get(\"from_seq\"), int) or pred.get(\"to_seq\") != seq \\\n                        or not 1 <= pred[\"from_seq\"] <= seq or pred != range_predicate(chain, pred[\"from_seq\"], seq):\n                    raise Bad(f\"anchors/{n}: attested range {pred!r} doesn't match this chain\")\n                ranges.append((pred[\"from_seq\"], seq, commit))\n                rows.append({\"anchor\": n, \"kind\": \"sigstore\", \"entries\": f\"{pred['from_seq']}-{seq}\", \"existed_by\": iso(t),\n                             \"writer_commit\": commit})","kind":"FileEditorAction"},"tool_name":"file_editor","tool_call_id":"file_editor_em8e4asv6ajf","tool_call":{"id":"file_editor_em8e4asv6ajf","name":"file_editor","arguments":"{\"command\": \"str_replace\", \"path\": \"/workspace/record/record.py\", \"old_str\": \"else:\\n                # Check if the corresponding .ots proof exists (should exist for each range head)\\n                ots_p